<div class="about-content">
    <h2>About Me</h2>
    <p class="lead">Hey, I'm Roberto Galdamez a first generation American born and raised in the heart of Jersey City.</p>
    
    <p>I recently graduated with a degree in Computer Science from New Jersey City University, and my path into tech has been anything but traditional. Growing up in an inner city neighborhood as the son of Honduran immigrants, I experienced firsthand the lack of access to resources and opportunities. But those challenges also sparked a deeper drive—to not only build a better life for myself but to help reshape the narrative around who belongs in tech.</p>
    
    <p>I'm passionate about full stack development and machine learning, and lately, I've been diving deeper into artificial intelligence—not just as a career path, but as a way to solve real world problems and push the boundaries of what's possible. My goal is to contribute to AI in a way that's ethical, accessible, and meaningful, especially for communities like the one I grew up in.</p>
    
    <p>As tech continues to shape every part of our lives, I've realized how few people truly understand the systems behind the screen. That gap—between the tech we use and the people who create itdrives me. I care deeply about expanding STEM education and helping young people, especially those battling depression, anxiety, or selfdoubt, realize they can thrive in this space too.</p>
    
    <p>Jersey City is becoming a growing tech hub, yet so many of the opportunities bypass the local community. I've seen the talent here, and I know what's possible when someone is given a chance. My journey is about more than just breaking into tech it's about making space for others to follow.</p>
</div>
